PRODUCT: {"name": "Hyundai CRETA", "category": "compact SUV", "summary": "A five-door, five-seat, front-wheel-drive compact SUV. The supplied September 2026 compilation lists three engines and ten trim columns.", "audience": "Buyers comparing everyday city use and longer journeys."}
BRAND: {"tone": "Warm, practical and restrained.", "voice_style": "Plain spoken English that translates supported features into ordinary situations.", "dos": ["Preserve exact trim and engine scope.", "Distinguish manufacturer descriptions from measured results.", "Keep unsupported questions as gaps."], "donts": ["Do not claim superiority or guarantees absent from evidence.", "Do not imply customer-specific context.", "Do not invent timing, mileage, capacity or safety results."], "persona_hint": "A product guide; inferred restrained profile, not an uploaded brand guideline."}
PLAN: {"customer_persona": "Everyday compact-SUV buyers comparing driving choices, passenger and luggage space, useful equipment and ownership costs. No individual route, budget, family, location or preferred trim is known unless the buyer supplies it.", "decision_frame": "The strongest fit is the engine and trim whose gearbox, seating and equipment match what you need, and the thing still to verify is that version\u2019s current on-road quote.", "takeaway": "Choose the engine and trim together, then check that exact version\u2019s features and current on-road quote.", "primary_outcome": "Identify an engine-and-trim combination to verify against the buyer\u2019s own requirements.", "supporting_outcomes": ["Understand the supported seating, assistance and comfort choices.", "Know which price, policy and measured evidence still need confirmation."], "concerns": [{"topic": "powertrain", "why": "The separate engines have different gearbox pairings, while fuel-use and performance measurements have not been supplied.", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009"]}, {"topic": "space-and-practicality", "why": "The split seat and rear recline explain arrangement choices but do not establish personal passenger, luggage or parking fit.", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F021", "F022", "F023", "F024", "F063"]}, {"topic": "safety", "why": "Standard airbags and selected-trim assistance establish equipment rather than a crash-test rating.", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F031", "F032", "F034"]}, {"topic": "ownership", "why": "The conflicting dated entry price is not a current local quote and extended petrol warranty is separately paid.", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"]}, {"topic": "running-costs", "why": "Measured fuel economy, service costs and resale evidence are missing.", "fact_ids": []}], "usps": [{"id": "choose-your-gears", "name": "Your choice of manual or automatic", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009"], "stop_id": "powertrain"}, {"id": "flexible-rear-room", "name": "Room that changes with your plans", "fact_ids": ["F022", "F023"], "stop_id": "space-and-practicality"}, {"id": "airbags-from-the-start", "name": "Airbags even on the starting trim", "fact_ids": ["F025"], "stop_id": "safety"}], "segments": [{"id": "opening", "title": "The button that holds the car still", "role": "intro", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Begin with the supported CRETA brake-holding function at a possible stop, naming the product fact before any scene and without greeting again. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 29-word alternative Browse intro uses F015/F016 for auto hold keeping a stationary car in place without the brake pedal staying pressed, identifying standard fit from King and keeping the separate S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatic-only rows deeper. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start on the literal AUTO HOLD button im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba, treat this as alternative opening material to the runtime overview, and hand off the choice of manual or automatic gearbox for the three-anchors segment with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 29}, {"id": "anchors", "title": "Your gearbox, rear seats and airbags", "role": "outcome", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Offer exactly three things to remember and state that the buyer can steer the tour without another question. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word alternative-opening batch names the three unchanged USP names using F003/F005/F006/F008/F009 for gearbox choice, F022/F023 for flexible seating and F025 for standard airbags, retaining engine-and-trim dependence and turbo automatic-only scope. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start on the manual lever im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455, change to folded rear seats im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde and the airbag diagram im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596, then hand off the non-turbo petrol engine as the first proof subject with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Choose which buying detail to explore", "topic": "highlights", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009", "F022", "F023", "F025"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears", "flexible-rear-room", "airbags-from-the-start"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455", "im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde", "im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 33}, {"id": "driving-choices", "title": "The petrol, diesel and turbo choices", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 opens on the non-turbo petrol engine and choosing how to change gears, B2 opens on considering diesel for the same possible journey, and B3 opens on the separate turbo engine and its trim constraint. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Reserve F015/F016 exclusively for the separate 23-word Explore overview, using the AUTO HOLD button and standard fit from King without repeating that claim in proof; allocate three 30-word proof batches to B1 F003/F009 for non-turbo petrol with manual or automatic depending on trim, B2 F003/F008 for diesel with manual or automatic depending on trim without a fuel-saving promise, and B3 F003/F005/F006 for automatic-only turbo petrol listed only on King while King also offers other engines, keeping complete F004/F007 quantities and F005/F008/F009 gearbox specifications deeper alongside F013/F014\u2019s exact automatic scopes and F002/F010/F011/F012 as manufacturer descriptions only. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use im_pdf_98cd4a320f9dbfd33bbd and the literal manual lever im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455 in B1, im_pdf_5cd207807990f4eea283 in B2 and im_pdf_87bac17ee980151549ba in B3, with handoffs explicitly to the diesel engine, the turbo engine and then the wheel-and-tyre choice, over 90 proof words with empty checkins and automatic selectors recorded as missing literal visuals.", "outcome": "Choose an engine and gearbox pairing", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F002", "F003", "F004", "F005", "F006", "F007", "F008", "F009", "F010", "F011", "F012", "F013", "F014", "F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": ["choose-your-gears"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_87bac17ee980151549ba", "im_pdf_5cd207807990f4eea283", "im_pdf_98cd4a320f9dbfd33bbd", "im_pdf_3aa2ebf1c9ed94570455", "im_pdf_893405c770ce75e06502", "im_pdf_82c706fa06eadf9268f7", "im_pdf_cf41d0e7be3699347595", "im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "powertrain", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 90}, {"id": "wheels", "title": "The wheel and tyre against the road", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the wheel design as an equipment choice and keep the question of road feel separate from its appearance. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 27-word batch uses F017 for steel or alloy options changing with trim, with the full wheel/trim mapping and F064 tyre dimensions held deeper and no clearance, suspension or comfort result inferred. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Begin on the literal alloy wheel and tyre im_pdf_a4463ebb4d4d6329f98a, whose spokes and visible caliper can be located without guessing wheel size, use im_pdf_3706b9e10eac9af2dac8 only for another wheel view, and hand off the split rear seatbacks where passengers and bags share space, with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Choose wheel style without inferring ride", "topic": "stance-and-ride", "fact_ids": ["F017", "F064"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_2f931aad60c08d1f4a9b", "im_pdf_689090f045758facf9e2", "im_pdf_fb2b4c4b8fb8583aaee6", "im_pdf_3706b9e10eac9af2dac8", "im_pdf_a4463ebb4d4d6329f98a"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "stance-and-ride", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 27}, {"id": "rear-space", "title": "The rear seatbacks and luggage space", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Begin with the visibly folded seatbacks when a possible trip includes both people and bags. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word batch uses F022/F023 for the standard split rear seat\u2019s passenger/storage flexibility and F021/F024 for rear passengers adjusting their seatback angle from S(O), while F001/F020/F059/F060/F063 and the complete split ratio stay deeper with no invented luggage capacity, legroom or personal-fit result; reserve F061 entirely for the supplemental storage batch. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde for literal folding, switch to im_pdf_74c2156461739f493698 only as contextual imagery for rear recline and use im_pdf_086219c79f5c77a4f468 only if sample luggage is mentioned, then hand off the airbags around the occupants\u2019 seats with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Arrange passenger seating and luggage together", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F020", "F021", "F022", "F023", "F024", "F059", "F060", "F061", "F063"], "usp_ids": ["flexible-rear-room"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_adb415f161dfc9567dde", "im_pdf_74c2156461739f493698", "im_pdf_086219c79f5c77a4f468", "im_pdf_31ed8989f6cc45b71b53", "im_pdf_06658fba292467f801c7"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "space-and-practicality", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 33}, {"id": "occupants-and-assistance", "title": "The airbags and help with traffic ahead", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 notices the airbag positions around the seats, while B2 considers the driver watching the vehicle ahead and separates assistance from responsibility. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Assign B1 32 words to F025 for six driver, passenger, side and curtain airbags fitted even on E, explaining that this equipment does not require buying a higher trim, and B2 32 words to F031/F032/F034 for forward-collision warning and assistance on King, King Knight and Lounge Edition with attentive-driver responsibility retained; hold F026\u2013F030/F033/F035/F036/F062 deeper with their exact standard, camera-from-SX-Premium and adaptive-stop-go-on-King/King-Knight/Lounge-automatics scopes and no inferred crash rating or stopping-distance result. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start B1 on the deployed-airbag illustration im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596 and B2 on the forward-detection illustration im_pdf_87d94ba1ddd0b388c716, hand off forward-collision assistance after B1 and the independent front temperature controls after B2, and use 64 total words with empty checkins, reserving the other safety pictures for their literal deeper subjects.", "outcome": "Distinguish standard equipment and selected assistance", "topic": "safety", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F026", "F027", "F028", "F029", "F030", "F031", "F032", "F033", "F034", "F035", "F036", "F062"], "usp_ids": ["airbags-from-the-start"], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_a54e8e56f4b50c2f5596", "im_pdf_97c32df6925fe7908b77", "im_pdf_87d94ba1ddd0b388c716", "im_pdf_76820ef14d297cc607b5", "im_pdf_debec8d7db7aa667b035", "im_pdf_beece6d09d55074c47bb", "im_pdf_c8743c0adbf32f9b7e56", "im_pdf_11d7b41540b2776d6e24"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "safety", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 64}, {"id": "front-controls", "title": "Two temperature settings and your phone", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 opens on the two displayed climate settings when the front occupants might prefer different temperatures, while B2 opens on connecting a compatible phone at the dashboard. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Assign B1 32 words to F039/F040 for driver and front passenger choosing their own settings from S(O), and B2 32 words to F045/F046 for compatible wireless Android Auto/Apple CarPlay from EX with the wired-to-wireless adapter condition retained on SX and above; hold F041/F042\u2019s complete screen dimensions, F043\u2019s three complimentary years and 70+ features with power/network conditions, F044\u2019s Alexa Home to Car from SX with separate hardware excluded, and F047\u2019s both-front power seats and driver memory from King deeper without claiming phone-app remote start. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use im_pdf_f14b998cc020fdfef1d5 for the literal climate panel and im_pdf_46a6d841c01356a2e42d only as contextual dashboard imagery for phone mirroring, never substituting the charging-pad photo as proof of that connection, then hand off the phone-and-screen connection after B1 and the airflow through front-seat cushions after B2 across 64 words with empty checkins.", "outcome": "Choose separate settings and compatible connection", "topic": "cabin-and-tech", "fact_ids": ["F039", "F040", "F041", "F042", "F043", "F044", "F045", "F046", "F047"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_46a6d841c01356a2e42d", "im_pdf_f14b998cc020fdfef1d5", "im_pdf_1a3e6160f7990cbb647c", "im_pdf_6fbbc0ada78471786303", "im_pdf_497f55977a7d19718157"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "cabin-and-tech", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 64}, {"id": "cabin-comforts", "title": "Airflow through the seats and the roof above", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 B1 notices airflow through the seat cushions on a possible warm evening, while B2 looks upward at the panoramic roof before the sound-system choice. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 B1 uses 31 words with F037/F038 for cool airflow through the front-seat cushions from SX Premium without a cooling-time or refrigerated-air claim; B2 uses 31 words with F048/F049 for a panoramic roof from EX(O), voice opening/closing from SX and F050 for Bose sound from SX Premium, keeping the full eight-speaker/subwoofer detail and F051/F052/F053\u2019s qualified lamp/glove-box choices deeper rather than adding a third batch. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Begin B1 on the literal airflow illustration im_pdf_498ba48d46b3d2258714, start B2 with the roof opening im_pdf_d3bdfccc9d80857379d1 and change to speaker locations im_pdf_bb10676bf859267f1262 when naming sound, explicitly hand off the roof and audio choice after B1 and the current on-road quote for the chosen version after B2, and keep all checkins empty within 62 words.", "outcome": "Choose seat airflow roof and audio", "topic": "delighters", "fact_ids": ["F037", "F038", "F048", "F049", "F050", "F051", "F052", "F053"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_498ba48d46b3d2258714", "im_pdf_bb10676bf859267f1262", "im_pdf_d3bdfccc9d80857379d1", "im_pdf_7df2ff055b2405e0a449", "im_pdf_7e1e6afe3e5807a60e62"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "delighters", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 62}, {"id": "current-quote", "title": "The price of the version you choose", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Begin with the honest limit that a starting amount does not settle a chosen version\u2019s local total. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 28-word batch uses F055/F056 to explain tax, registration and insurance added to the ex-showroom amount and the dealer\u2019s current itemised quote, holding F054\u2019s 19 September 2026 entry amount of \u20b910,90,700 and conflicting \u20b910.79 lakh structured value together in deeper and reserving F057/F058 for establish only. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use the whole-car side profile im_pdf_689090f045758facf9e2 as explicitly contextual imagery because no quotation image exists, then hand off the front-armrest storage detail still to consider alongside the equipment choice, with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Confirm a current itemised on-road quote", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_689090f045758facf9e2"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "ownership", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 28}, {"id": "front-storage", "title": "The storage beside your seat", "role": "features", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the open front-armrest compartment as a place for everyday small items without asserting that any particular object fits. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 26-word batch uses F061 for standard front-armrest storage and sliding adjustment from King, whose supported continuous run is King, King Knight and Lounge Edition, without adding capacity, cooling or locking claims. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start on the literal open compartment im_pdf_06658fba292467f801c7, use im_pdf_25b7515fe0c9e93714e1 only for the closed front-armrest context, and hand off the selected engine/trim and its written warranty terms, counting this as space-and-practicality\u2019s second batch with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Locate storage and optional armrest adjustment", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F061"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_06658fba292467f801c7", "im_pdf_25b7515fe0c9e93714e1"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 26}, {"id": "written-terms", "title": "The version and paperwork to confirm", "role": "establish", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Keep the engine and trim together as the buyer moves from equipment to the written terms and missing evidence. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 One 33-word batch gives the variant-choice instruction, voices F057/F058\u2019s separately paid petrol-only extended warranty, and identifies missing engine-specific fuel-economy figures and the exact-model/year crash-test report with official Hyundai certification information and the applicable testing body\u2019s report as their resolving sources; keep the up-to-seven-years warranty limit, absent package prices/coverage, local stock and delivery deeper without repeating the price claim. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Hold the whole-car exterior im_pdf_2f931aad60c08d1f4a9b solely as contextual imagery, never policy or road-test proof, then hand off the supported engine/equipment fit and unresolved current quote to the final summary and dealer-contact action, counting this as ownership\u2019s second batch with an empty checkin.", "outcome": "Identify written terms and unresolved evidence", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im_pdf_2f931aad60c08d1f4a9b"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 33}], "ctas": [{"id": "dealer-contact", "label": "Request dealer contact", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": true, "when": "end"}, {"id": "test-drive-contact", "label": "Request a test drive", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": false, "when": "end"}], "voice": {"persona_name": "Priya", "persona_description": "The guide is a practical product guide who pays attention to the buyer\u2019s questions. The guide explains one useful thought at a time, with warmth and candour about missing evidence.", "tone": "Cheerful, attentive Indian English with everyday words, short connected thoughts and restrained pauses.", "sample_line": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "suggested_voice": "priya", "language": "en-IN"}, "intake": {"q1": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "q2": "", "chips": [{"key": "powertrain", "label": "Engines and gears"}, {"key": "stance-and-ride", "label": "Wheels and roads"}, {"key": "space-and-practicality", "label": "Seats and luggage"}, {"key": "safety", "label": "Safety and assistance"}, {"key": "cabin-and-tech", "label": "Controls and phone"}, {"key": "delighters", "label": "Seat airflow and roof"}, {"key": "ownership", "label": "Price and ownership"}]}, "do_not_recommend_if": "Do not recommend a specific version while a non-negotiable requirement depends on missing fuel-economy, safety-test, personal-fit, price or availability evidence.", "advance": "When the buyer wants to verify a version, offer Request dealer contact so the selected Hyundai dealer can confirm the engine and trim and supply a current itemised on-road quotation; selecting the CTA records a contact preference and optional follow-up, not completed contact or booking.", "notes": "Explore overview reservation: F015/F016 only, 23 words, using im_pdf_e1266b7974b364c1c1ba for the AUTO HOLD button and its stationary brake-holding function standard from King; keep S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatic-only availability and the S(O) Knight current-combination caveat in deeper, and do not voice auto hold again in guided proof. The overview hands off the non-turbo petrol engine, the first proof subject. Intro/outcome are alternative Browse opening material, not additions to Explore. Guided main allocation is 427 words: powertrain 30+30+30, wheels 27, space 33, safety 32+32, cabin 32+32, delighters 31+31, price 28, supplemental storage 26 and establish 33. These 14 main batches are each 26\u201333 words; the 23-word overview and 45-word closing yield the full 495-word target. Powertrain receives three proof batches; space totals two including storage and ownership totals two including establish; other stops stay at most two. Two closing statements only, both in the final 45-word block: supported fit without an invented preferred trim, then Request dealer contact with its actual recording semantics. All segment checkins are empty. Every handoff names the next actual subject and each batch stands alone after interruption. Seven Coach stops and three USP objects are unchanged; no playbook version was supplied. Use the supplied picture descriptions to reject mismatched fact-level suggestions: a tablet is not phone mirroring, a camera display is not a sensor, front storage is not a rear armrest, and engine illustrations are not wheelbase evidence. Technical quantities stay complete in deeper; no calculated differences or unsupported felt outcomes. The configured Sarvam Priya identity is retained. Unknown customer context stays unknown and all action URLs remain empty because no destination was supplied.", "total_words": 495, "playbook_version": "2026-09-23", "guided_minimum_seconds": 180.0, "guided_opening_words": 23, "narration_preparation": {"version": 1, "target_words": 495, "identity": "87410a51f3aa29c066e33422e66f2ec496d2673272bacf6c6840265fa9ff11db"}}

FACT REGISTRY — the only allowed source of facts:
F001 [spec·stated] Body and driveline: five-door, five-seat compact SUV (conditions: All variants; manufacturer compilation dated 19 September 2026) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "The Hyundai CRETA is a five-door, five-seat compact SUV built by Hyundai Motor India and sold with front-wheel\ndrive across the whole range.")
F002 [claim·stated] Intended use: city use while still being capable on longer runs (conditions: Manufacturer positioning; not measured superiority) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "Hyundai positions the car as an SUV that works for city use while still being capable on longer runs.")
F003 [spec·stated] Engine choice: 1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 4; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol")
F004 [spec·stated] Turbo maximum power: 117.5 kW (160 PS) @ 5,500 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol; specification, not an acceleration measurement) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min")
F005 [spec·stated] Turbo transmission: 7-speed DCT (conditions: Turbo petrol only; DCT means dual-clutch automatic) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol\n1,482 cm³\n117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min\n253 Nm (25.8 kgm) @\n1,500–3,500 r/min\n7-speed DCT")
F006 [availability·stated] Turbo trim availability: King (conditions: Column headers E, EX, EX(O), S(O), S(O) Knight, SX, SX Premium, King, King Knight, Lounge Edition. Only King is marked for turbo/DCT. King also offers other engines; do not imply every King is turbo.) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 31; quote: "1.5 l turbo GDi petrol\nDCT\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n ●\n –\n –")
F007 [spec·stated] Diesel torque: 250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @ 1,500–2,750 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; not a loaded-climb performance test) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min")
F008 [spec·stated] Diesel transmission choices: 6-speed manual or 6-speed automatic (conditions: Trim combinations differ; see engine matrix page 31) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel\n1,493 cm³\n85 kW (116 PS) @ 4,000\nr/min\n250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min\n6-speed manual or\n6-speed automatic")
F009 [spec·stated] Petrol transmission choices: 6-speed manual or IVT (conditions: Naturally aspirated petrol; trim combinations differ) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol\n1,497 cm³\n84.4 kW (115 PS) @ 6,300\nr/min\n143.8 Nm (14.7 kgm) @ 4,500\nr/min\n6-speed manual or IVT")
F010 [claim·stated] Turbo manufacturer driving description: impressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling (conditions: Hyundai marketing description, not a measured test result; never imply an acceleration time or guaranteed overtaking) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It delivers\nimpressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling for a thrilling yet refined drive across city roads and\nhighways alike")
F011 [claim·stated] Diesel manufacturer driving description: strong torque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance (conditions: Hyundai marketing, not mileage or noise measurements) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "The robust 1.5L U2 CRDi diesel engine, available with 6-speed manual and automatic transmissions, delivers strong\ntorque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance.")
F012 [claim·stated] Petrol manufacturer use description: everyday practicality with refined driving comfort (conditions: Hyundai marketing. Do not convert superior fuel economy to a comparative test or mileage figure.) (source: src_0ac142; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It combines everyday practicality with refined driving comfort, ensuring consistent\npower delivery and superior fuel economy.")
